# Network topology:
# Sources: 1, 2, 3
# Sinks: 13, 14
# Bottleneck zones: zone A (to node 8), zone B (to node 9), then cross-coupled late-stage mixing.
# Fork nodes: 1, 2, 3, 8, 9, 10, 12
# Join nodes: 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12
# Parallel path groups: multiple parallel routes from each source set to sinks through {8,9}->{10,11}->{12,13,14}.
# Designed behavior: nontrivial min-cut lattice, meaningful k=2 failures, and distributed sensitivity (not single-edge dominance).
